The following offenses are to be handled by the department from which the respondent belongs to. The College Discipline Board will handle the third commission of any first-degree offense.
1. Shouting, loud voices, boisterous conduct or any action that causes disturbances;
2. Using sound amplification equipment such as bullhorn on campus or in a campus building without written permission of the Vice President for Student Affairs and Services or the VPSAS’ designee;
3. Writing, drawing or posting physically or online of any medium for malicious purposes;
4. Attending classes not wearing the prescribed uniform, wearing incomplete uniform, wearing the uniform improperly;
5. Smoking inside the campus;
6. Use of indecent or malicious words / act against fellow students;

7. Possessing, displaying, distributing pornographic materials (pictures, posters, slides, CDs, VCDs, DVDs or similar materials), writing pornographic literature, accessing pornographic materials through school facilities (i.e. internet access in the library, study area), including personal devices such as cell phones, iPods, iPads, tablets, laptops, PSP, etc.;
8. Discourteous and disruptive use of cellular phones during classes;
9. Misuse or tampering identification card;
10. Willfully refusing to, or falsely identifying oneself, willfully failing to comply with a proper order or summons when requested by an authorized university official;
11. Violating other university, college, department and organization regulations which have been posted or publicized;

12. Unauthorized entry upon the playing performance area or the spectators’ area of any academic, cultural or athletic contest, exhibition or other event;
13. Littering anywhere in the campus;
14. Loitering along corridors during class hours;
15. Violating the school canteen’s Clean As You Go (CLAYGO) policy;
16. Posting of unauthorized notice and / or announcements on bulletin boards & UB official social media accounts or posting of tarpaulins, streamers in the school area; (Note: The Corporate Communications Office of the university generally regulates Posting of announcements)
17. For male students: wearing earrings, headgear and/ or other accessories inappropriate for school wear unless authorized for specific function/ activities;
18. For female students: wearing more than one (1) set of earrings and/ or other accessories inappropriate for school wear;

1. Brawl inside the campus or within the vicinity of the University;
2. Gambling inside the campus;
3. Carrying of deadly weapons or explosives inside the campus;
4. Showing disrespect, threatening or endangering the health, safety or welfare of faculty members or other school personnel (physical, verbal, written or posted online);
5. Vandalism (destroying school properties such as fire alarm, firefighting equipment, doors, windows, desks, tables, etc);
6. Intentionally making a false report of a bomb, fire, natural disaster or other emergency to a University official or an emergency service agency;
7. Altering, forging, misusing university records or documents;
8. Submission of false records of academic achievement to obtain grades, honors, awards or professional endorsement;
9. Acquiring or using testing materials without faculty permission;

10. Wrongful or unauthorized use of University properties or facilities;
11. Unlawful taking, wrongful sale or gift of property belonging to the University to a member of the University community, guest, or anybody;
12. Commission of any three first-degree offenses whether of a similar nature or otherwise may be elevated as a major offense depending on the nature of the offense and the guild of the offender;
13. Any forms of bullying (verbal, physical or cyber) committed by a student against another student, faculty member or any school personnel;

1. Academic Dishonesty including but not limited to plagiarism, fabrication of data, deception, and sabotage of the work of others;
2. Unauthorized bringing, possession or use of liquor or illegal drugs;
3. Attending classes or school activities under the influence of alcohol and/ or illegal drugs;
4. Physically assaulting faculty members and or other school personnel whether in or off the campus;
5. Participation in hazing whether as the person joining an organization or the one conducting the hazing (other students who are also present at hazing / initiation are also liable whether or not they actually participate in hazing/ initiation;
6. Sexual harassment, sexual misconduct and other similar immoral acts that may negatively affect the good reputation of the school;
